# issue: none
# notes: one 60-doc fixture, two edge types, three filter positions beside a hop.
# notes: Knows leaves 10, 20, 30, 40, 50 (5 of 60 = 8.3%, gate prefilters); Likes
# notes: leaves every 5th doc from 5 (11 of 60 = 18%, Threshold fallback).
# notes: Step 1 `$d.n > 15  $d knows $t`, limit 2: the pushed filter AND the
# notes: gate's id list on one scan; 20, 30, 40, 50 survive both (4 > 2): d020,
# notes: d030. Step 2 `$d knows $t  $t.n > 25`, limit 2: the target filter cannot
# notes: be pushed, the gate's ids over-admit (10 and 20 have targets 11, 21),
# notes: the first prefiltered pass holds 10, 20 and loses both; the overfetch
# notes: rerun under the same id list reaches 30, 40, 50 (3 > 2): d030, d040.
# notes: Step 3 `$d.n > 15  $d likes $t`, limit 2: above the fence, so the
# notes: filter is pushed and the traversal drops rows above an unfiltered scan;
# notes: k 2 (16, 17) and 8 (16..23: one source, 20) are short, k 32 fills:
# notes: d020, d025. Three different answers, one per path.

--- schema
node Doc {
    slug: String @key
    n: I64 @index
    name: String @index
    embedding: Vector(4) @index
}

edge Knows: Doc -> Doc {
}

edge Likes: Doc -> Doc {
}

